# Node Standards

## General Rules

- Every node must have a descriptive name (no default "HTTP Request1" names)
- Every non-trivial node must have a sticky note explaining its purpose
- Pinned test data is required for nodes that fetch external data

## Node-Specific Standards

### HTTP Request
- Always set timeout (default: 30000ms)
- Always handle 4xx and 5xx responses explicitly
- Use `$credentials` for authentication, never hardcode tokens

### Code (JavaScript)
- Follow @n8n-code-javascript skill standards
- Max 50 lines per Code node — split into multiple nodes if longer
- Always return an array of objects

### IF / Switch
- Document each branch with a sticky note
- Default/fallback branch is mandatory

### AI Agent
- Follow @ai-agent-standards.mdc
- Always set a system prompt
- Define tools explicitly — no open-ended tool access

### Set / Edit Fields
- Use dot notation for nested fields
- Document the purpose of each field being set

### Error Trigger
- Every workflow must have one
- Connect to a notification node (Slack, email, or webhook)
